              "<details><summary>[LLIS 614] GSE Test Rig Installation</summary><p><a href=\"https://llis.nasa.gov/lesson/614\" target=\"_blank\">Open original record</a></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">DRIVING EVENT\n",
              "While performing a functional retest of a Shuttle hatch movement, following a hatch actuator R&amp;R, the GSE support structure failed. As a result, the hatch hinges and hinge arm mechanism were potentially subjected to the full unsupported weight of the hatch.\n",
              "\n",
              "LESSON\n",
              "Hatch support GSE had been installed incorrectly (90 degrees from correct position).\n",
              "\n",
              "RECOMMENDATION\n",
              "Design and fabricate GSE support equipment so that it can be installed only in one way, with no options.</pre></details>"
